venv/

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Secrets. The CourtListener API token is read from the environment, never
# committed. See governance/source-register.md.
.env

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE DATA FREEZE, AND WHY PART OF IT IS NOT COMMITTED
#
# Every prior Cascadia module commits data/raw/ outright, because an EDGAR
# response is a few hundred kilobytes. This module's snapshot is a 314 MB zip
# that expands to 2.0 GB of tab-delimited text, and git is the wrong container
# for it.
#
# The freeze is therefore asserted by HASH, not by tracking the bytes:
# data/raw/cv88on.zip.sha256 and governance/source-register.md are committed
# and are the authoritative record of what was pulled and when.
# src/validate_freeze.py re-computes the hash and fails if it moved.
#
# Everything DERIVED from the snapshot -- data/reference/ and data/conformed/
# -- is committed, and is small.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/raw/cv88on.zip
data/raw/*.txt
data/raw/*.part
